WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.240
- Hey, we're Rhett and Link.

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:02.340
- We're here at Buzzfeed and today

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:03.660
we're gonna be answering some questions

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:05.450
about our first times.
- Ooh.

00:00:06.051 --> 00:00:08.551
(jazzy music)

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:10.280
I'll open it for you, make it easier.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:14.263
- Okay, first AIM or AOL account name.

00:00:14.923 --> 00:00:16.160
Oh man.
- I remember

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:19.350
I had one that had it was all consonants.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:24.350
R-H-T-T-M-C-G-H-L-N.

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:29.200
- You could've said that faster.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:32.750
My first AOL username was Leaky Faucet

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:34.900
with like three numbers after it.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:37.063
- Linky faucet?
- Leaky faucet.

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:38.520
- Well that was a missed opportunity.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:39.870
- Now I know the answer to the question,

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:41.270
if you could go back in time

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:42.810
and change anything, what would it be?

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:45.490
It would be my AOL username
to make it more punny.

00:00:45.490 --> 00:00:46.343
Next question.

00:00:46.487 --> 00:00:48.570
(jazzy music)

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:50.640
First big purchase as a YouTuber.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.800
- Oh, Lambo.
- This is a funny (laughs).

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:56.960
So we uploaded a video to YouTube in 2006

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:58.100
when YouTube started.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.053
And then I probably went
out and bought some,

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:01.610
I don't know, some saltines.

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:06.610
- You're forgetting we
bought a Scion together.

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:10.430
- Yeah we went in on a Scion.

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:13.563
- We went to the bank, we
got all the cash we had,

00:01:13.945 --> 00:01:14.778
because--
- Literally.

00:01:14.778 --> 00:01:15.611
We got bills.
- Because somebody told us

00:01:15.611 --> 00:01:16.444
you need to buy in cash.

00:01:16.444 --> 00:01:18.080
We didn't know that that meant that--

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:19.880
- You just paid for it.
- You just paid in full.

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:23.840
We literally brought an
envelope full of $18,000,

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:26.130
which I think is technically
illegal to carry around.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:28.320
- I was gonna follow it
up at the bank teller

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:31.010
and say well can I have it all in ones

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:33.263
and can I get a briefcase?

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:34.880
And it still probably
wouldn't have been enough

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:37.560
to justify a briefcase,
more just like a lunch sack.

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:39.210
- Yeah it would've been annoying, too.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:41.110
- First thing you do when you wake up.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:43.750
- Roll over, I pick up my phone,

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:46.250
and build my self-image
from the YouTube comments.

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:50.773
- First thing I do when
I wake up is roll over,

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:53.860
see if Rhett's texted me
because his self-image

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:55.853
has been shattered by YouTube comments.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.023
- Yep, every day.

00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:00.883
- First time being recognized in public.

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:03.803
Still kinda hoping for that.

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:05.700
Still kinda looking around.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:09.433
I frequently go up to
people and I'm like so.

00:02:09.816 --> 00:02:13.143
(crickets chirping)
Me, my face.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:14.963
Ring any bells?

00:02:15.304 --> 00:02:17.120
(crickets chirping)

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:18.493
YouTube much?

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:21.630
- I remember a time I
was out with my family

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:26.343
and we ran into my grandmother.

00:02:27.845 --> 00:02:30.245
She was like didn't expect
to see you guys here.

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:32.160
- But she knew it was you.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:33.760
- She recognized us right off the bat.

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:35.303
The whole family, all of us.

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:39.343
- And the last one, first pet.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:43.293
My first pet was a dog named Tucker.

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:45.193
He was brown and shaggy.

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:46.660
- I remember the day he died.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:49.470
- Yeah, we--
- Performed a funeral for him.

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:52.230
- We buried him in a refrigerator
box 'cause he was huge.

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:54.380
It rained a lot the next
day and the whole grave

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:57.410
filled with mud and--
- We jumped into it.

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:58.483
- We jumped into it.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:01.760
- My first pet was Pokey, a hamster,

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.220
that got lost for a month

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:05.950
and we found him inside of
a sleeping bag in my closet

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:08.233
and he had been living off of the fibers.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:09.890
- He'd been eating the sleeping bag?

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:10.723
- Yeah.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:12.880
He lived for another year.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.190
We're Rhett and Link, we
enjoyed answering questions

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:16.370
about our first time.

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:18.870
- Please check out our
show Good Mythical Morning,

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:21.050
every weekday on YouTube.

00:03:21.165 --> 00:03:23.332
(echoing)

00:03:24.565 --> 00:03:27.065
(jazzy music)

